{
  "id": "celery_celery_10519",
  "repo_name": "celery/celery",
  "repo_url": "https://github.com/celery/celery",
  "base_commit": "7c846b63b10eb296e310625104e5d0ccf672d85c",
  "pr_number": 10519,
  "issue_number": 10517,
  "issue_title": "LocalTimezone.fromutc corrupts offsets for negative-UTC-offset locales (timedelta.seconds discards sign)",
  "issue_body": "## Summary\n\n`celery.utils.time.LocalTimezone.fromutc()` computes the UTC offset using `timedelta.seconds`, which is always normalized to `0..86399` with the sign carried by `timedelta.days`. For any locale whose UTC offset is **negative** (entire western hemisphere), the computed offset flips sign and inflates to up to `+23:59`, corrupting every UTC\u2192local conversion made through this tzinfo by up to ~24 hours.\n\nThis path is active when `enable_utc=False` (the class docstring states it is used only then), which is also the fallback taken when `tzlocal.get_localzone()` fails (bare containers, missing `/etc/localtime`, broken `TZ`) \u2014 i.e., exactly the environments most likely to silently hit it.\n\nReproduced empirically on a US-Eastern-style zone:\n\n```python\nSTDOFFSET = timedelta(hours=-5); DSTOFFSET = timedelta(hours=-4)\nlt = LocalTimezone()\nlt.fromutc(datetime(2026, 6, 15, 12, 0))\n# -> datetime(2026, 6, 16, 7, 0, tzinfo=timezone(+19:00))   WRONG (+20h shift)\n# expected: datetime(2026, 6, 15, 8, 0, tzinfo=timezone(-04:00))\n```\n\n*Note: reproduced in isolation against the current `main` source; not run inside a live worker.*\n\n## Location\n\n- File: `celery/utils/time.py`\n- Class/function: `LocalTimezone.fromutc`\n- Relevant code path:\n\n```python\ndef fromutc(self, dt: datetime) -> datetime:\n    # The base tzinfo class no longer implements a DST\n    # offset aware .fromutc() in Python 3 (Issue #2306).\n    offset = int(self.utcoffset(dt).seconds / 60.0)\n    try:\n        tz = self._offset_cache[offset]\n    except KeyError:\n        tz = self._offset_cache[offset] = datetime_timezone(\n            timedelta(minutes=offset))\n    return tz.fromutc(dt.replace(tzinfo=tz))\n```\n\n## Problem\n\nFor a `-04:00` zone, `self.utcoffset(dt)` returns `timedelta(days=-1, seconds=72000)` (Python normalizes so `.seconds \u2208 [0, 86399)` and the sign lives in `.days`). Dividing `.seconds` by 60 yields `+1200` minutes instead of `-240`. `datetime.timezone(timedelta(minutes=1200))` is a `+20:00` zone, so `fromutc` shifts UTC instants forward by 20 hours instead of back by 4.\n\nPositive-offset zones work only by accident (their `.days == 0`). Negative-offset zones get:\n\n- wrong wall-clock rendering everywhere this tzinfo is used (crontab matching, beat displays, `to_local` conversions),\n- flipped DST classification (`_isdst` evaluated on the corrupted local time),\n- an unbounded-growth `_offset_cache` keyed by minute values like `1200`, `1140`, \u2026 rather than the real few distinct offsets.\n\n## Steps to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport time as _time\nfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta\n_time.timezone = 4 * 3600        # simulate UTC-4 std\n_time.daylight = 1; _time.altzone = 5 * 3600\n_time.tzname = (\"EST\", \"EDT\"); _time.tzset = lambda: None\n\nimport celery.utils.time as cut\nltz = cut.LocalTimezone()\nprint(ltz.fromutc(datetime(2026, 6, 15, 12, 0)))\n# 2026-06-16 07:00:00+19:00  <- should be 2026-06-15 08:00:00-04:00\n```\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\n`fromutc` should apply the true signed offset: `-04:00` for a summer US-Eastern instant.\n\n## Actual Behavior\n\nOffset sign is lost and magnitude wraps into `[0, 24h)`, producing local times up to a day off.\n\n## Impact\n\nSilent schedule skew across all western-hemisphere deployments running with `enable_utc=False` (and any environment where the tzlocal fallback engages): beat fires crontab entries relative to a shifted clock, logs/monitoring show times ~a day in the future/past, and eta/countdown conversions misalign. Because the corruption is deterministic per-offset, it will look like a consistent \"future-dated\" task bug rather than a timezone failure.\n\n## Suggested Direction\n\nOne-line fix \u2014 use the full signed value:\n\n```python\noffset = int(self.utcoffset(dt).total_seconds() // 60)\n```\n\nOptionally clamp/cache on the resulting minutes (which will then be the real handful of offsets). A regression test constructing `LocalTimezone` under negative `_time.timezone` and asserting `fromutc` round-trips would pin it.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Quoted code is verbatim from `main`; note `__init__` correctly computes `STDOFFSET = timedelta(seconds=-_time.timezone)` (line 81), so the intent was clearly a signed value that `.seconds` then discards.\n- Reachability: class docstring (\"Used only when the :setting:`enable_utc` setting is disabled\") and the `LocalTimezone()` fallback construction in `_Zone.local`.\n- Dedup searches for `LocalTimezone`, `fromutc`, `utcoffset seconds` across issues/PRs surface only unrelated hits (#9862 tzlocal ordering, #10344 spring-forward gap).\n",
  "merged_at": "2026-08-26T15:25:02Z",
